false, "score": 24, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8789196, "raw_content": "", "author": "crowsfury", "created": 1787191323457, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "ColonelKlink", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCIrk0Ck.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/MikeRogersForMI/status/2090088423323279769", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "In his own words, Abdul El-Sayed called for a government takeover of health insurance because health insurance has \"no value\". He says taxes will have to be raised and it makes sense that \"everybody pays a bit in\".", "last_comment_created": 1787191804825, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 24, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 227, "created": 1787150886000, "id": "2090088423323279769", "video": {"preview": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2090088314753654784/img/CaV98GG2RVb3bBjl.jpg", "mpeg": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2090088314753654784/pl/heROidg6pDXZye3E.m3u8?v=829", "aspectRatio": [16, 9], "heightRatio": 56, "type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2090088314753654784/vid/avc1/480x270/9jh4aiFz29pjbjXh.mp4"}, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1722766729829326848/6sMh_dR9_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Mike Rogers", "username": "MikeRogersForMI"}, "content": "Abdul El-Sayed is a snake oil salesman. \n\nHe wants to take away your doctor and take money out of your pocket.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 1323}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCIrk0Ci", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 24, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8789194, "raw_content": "Not even anything to do with alcohol specifically. It\u2019s the first of the amendments that isn\u2019t a negative right or changing the structure of government. It\u2019s just a ban on something that the people could already do. Horrible precedent. The other amendments either ban the government from infringing your natural rights, or modify the process of government. But none of them before that broke the spirit of the Constitution in the same way. Even the 14th amendment, which while I think there are a few good points, I overall think was horribly written in general. But that\u2019s a different debate. But the 18th basically set the precedent that the federal government is all powerful, and your rights to do things can be taken away, rights that were stated to be natural and inborn. Not a coincidence that the worst president in US history, Woodrow Wilson, was in office when it passed. That is the start of modern progressivism. And it\u2019s where the entire idea of everything being a right \u201cgranted\u201d by the government comes from. Instead of our rights existing and we the people forcing the government to respect them. The modern left largely operates from the same point of view that the people who passed the 18th amendment did. ", "author": "lefty295", "created": 1787191313002, "profile_picture": "NWbNd6AomP4v", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "lefty295", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Around the passage of the 18th amendment is when the government of this country completely lost the plot and took a big shit on our rights. It\u2019s a huge stain on our constitution.", "last_comment_created": 1787192086881, "content": "<p>Not even anything to do with alcohol specifically. It\u2019s the first of the amendments that isn\u2019t a negative right or changing the structure of government. It\u2019s just a ban on something that the people could already do. Horrible precedent. The other amendments either ban the government from infringing your natural rights, or modify the process of government. But none of them before that broke the spirit of the Constitution in the same way. Even the 14th amendment, which while I think there are a few good points, I overall think was horribly written in general. But that\u2019s a different debate. But the 18th basically set the precedent that the federal government is all powerful, and your rights to do things can be taken away, rights that were stated to be natural and inborn. Not a coincidence that the worst president in US history, Woodrow Wilson, was in office when it passed. That is the start of modern progressivism. And it\u2019s where the entire idea of everything being a right \u201cgranted\u201d by the government comes from. Instead of our rights existing and we the people forcing the government to respect them. The modern left largely operates from the same point of view that the people who passed the 18th amendment did.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 1, "score_up": 24, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2090073663835935206", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATC